<title>USA: Genemedicine to start trial on cancer drug.</title>
<headline>Genemedicine to start trial on cancer drug.</headline>
<dateline>THE WOODLANDS, Texas 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>GeneMedicine Inc said Monday it has received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to start the Phase I clinical trial for its Interleukin-2 (IL-2) cancer gene medicine that is being developed for the treatment of head and neck cancer.</p>
<p>GeneMedicine said it expects starting the trial in the first half of 1997 to study the safety and tolerability of the product.</p>
<p>It said it filed an Investigational New Drug Application (IND) for IL-2 in December 1996.</p>
</text>
